#%RAML 1.0 DataType
(package): Project
type: string
(beta): true
displayName: ProductCatalogModel
description: |
  Determines how Product Variants are managed in the Project.
(enumDescriptions):
  Classic: Product Variants are embedded in the Product. This is the default behavior.
  InMigration: Product Variants remain embedded in the Product and Variant update actions on the Product API are still accepted, but resources that reference a Variant, such as [Carts](/projects/carts) and Order line items, discount matching, and Product Selections, resolve from modular Variants by default. Use this transitional state to migrate your reads to the Modular Catalog model while embedded Variant writes continue.
  Modular: Product Variants are managed as standalone entities through the Variants endpoint. Variant-related update actions on Products are not available in this mode. Pricing is exclusively handled through [StandalonePrices](ctp:api:type:StandalonePrice); [Embedded Prices](ctp:api:type:Price) are not supported.
enum:
  - Classic
  - InMigration
  - Modular
